cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below. This citation covers
  the conversion tools only, not the models. If you use one of the converted models
  published on Hugging Face, please also cite its original authors, as given on its model
  card: https://huggingface.co/collections/Valen-Peregrine/faunapulse-6ad22f04766aed6641688544
title: "Tools to convert and quantise detection and identification models for the FaunaPulse app"
abstract: >-
  Python tools, run on a computer, that convert animal detection and identification models
  into LiteRT (.tflite) files for FaunaPulse, an Android app that detects, tracks and
  identifies animals on the phone itself. The tools convert Ultralytics YOLO detectors
  (segmentation models such as flat-bug become box detectors), the insectDCT hierarchical
  classifier and the image encoders of BioCLIP 1, 2 and 2.5. They quantise the files to make
  them smaller (fp16, 8-bit weights, or, for detectors, full INT8, which needs calibration
  images) and compare a converted file's outputs with those of the original PyTorch model.
  They also build label packs: lists of taxon names, taken from the BioCLIP authors'
  TreeOfLife-200M list, that BioCLIP can choose from on the phone. An upload script
  publishes the converted files on Hugging Face, each with a model card. The tools
  are designed for any supported model, including detectors that users train themselves.
  The models published so far were trained by others: each model card names their original authors and
  how to cite them. The conversions are unofficial, not provided or endorsed by the original
  authors. This repository holds the code and the texts of the model cards, not the model
  files, which are on Hugging Face.
